with ≥2 of the following risk factors for atrial fibrillation:\n - age ≥75 years\n - female sex\n - obstructive sleep apnea\n - peripheral vascular disease\n - diabetes mellitus\n - obesity (body mass index [BMI] >30 kg/m2)\n - hypertension\n - congestive heart failure\nExclusion Criteria:\n - prior diagnosis of AF\n - continuous rhythm monitoring over the past year\n - pacemaker [OR] or implantable cardioverter defibrillator in situ<|eot_id|>']
Response: Inclusion Criteria:
Nursing home residents with ≥2 of the following risk factors for atrial fibrillation:
 - age ≥75 years
 - female sex
 - obstructive sleep apnea
 - peripheral vascular disease
 - diabetes mellitus
 - obesity (body mass index [BMI] >30 kg/m2)
 - hypertension
 - congestive heart failure
Exclusion Criteria:
 - prior diagnosis of AF
 - continuous rhythm monitoring over the past year
 - pacemaker [OR] or implantable cardioverter defibrillator in situ
